For context if it helps, here is the latest extended message from Carmen

> Begin forwarded message:
>=20
> From: Carmen Brando Lebas <carmen.brando@gmail.com>
> Subject: RE : hello again and Alcedo/TopUrbi
> Date: March 23, 2026 at 5:01:19=E2=80=AFAM MDT
> To: Karl Grossner <karl.geog@gmail.com>, Karl Grossner =
<karl@kgeographer.org>
>=20
> Hi Karl,
>=20
> Thank you, glad to hear from you =E2=80=94 I hope things are well to =
you and yours too!
>=20
> Werner has now completed the work on the Alcedo dictionary within the =
TopUrbi project, covering both the TEI digital edition and the =
historical place gazetteer.
> Jean-Paul Zu=C3=B1iga (TopUrbi's PI) and Werner have both been in =
touch with Gimena del Rio on this.
> One key difference from Gimena's original approach is that we chose to =
work from the original Spanish edition, whereas Gimena mentioned she had =
started with an English translation.
> Starting from the Spanish meant essentially beginning from scratch, =
which took up Werner's full two-year contract within TopUrbi.
>=20
> Please note that the repository you found is no longer active and the =
data there is outdated. The current resources =E2=80=94 scripts, data, =
TEI Publisher app (still in progress), and bibliographic references =E2=80=
=94 are in our main repository: =
https://gitlab.huma-num.fr/plateforme-geomatique-et-hn/topurbi-project =
(the second part of the README is in English)
>=20
> The most up-to-date gazetteer data is in the TEI index here:
> =
https://gitlab.huma-num.fr/plateforme-geomatique-et-hn/topurbi-data/-/tree=
/main/auxiliary?ref_type=3Dheads=20
>=20
> On the question of data sharing: TopUrbi was funded by the French =
National Research Agency (ANR), which requires us to make our data FAIR.
> We chose an open licence with a non-commercial restriction =E2=80=94 =
CC BY-NC 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/). Would =
this be compatible with WHG's requirements?
>=20
> We are also required to systematically cite the project by its full =
name and code: ANR TopUrbi =E2=80=94 Topographie de l'urbanisation =
imp=C3=A9riale hispanique (Projet-ANR-21-CE27-0023). Ideally, I would =
like this attribution to appear at the record level in WHG =E2=80=94 is =
that something that could be arranged?
>=20
> Contributing our gazetteer to WHG has been part of my plan from the =
beginning. I was hoping to convert the data to the WHG format, but since =
Werner's departure I've had to take care of several things we hadn't =
finished. We are currently working with JINNTEC to customise and improve =
the TEI Publisher site for the dictionary.
>=20
> If you have a workflow to facilitate the conversion to the WHG data =
model, that would be a great help.
>=20
> Werner mentioned that you both previously imported the HGIS de las =
Indias into WHG =E2=80=94 I would like to do the same for the TopUrbi =
gazetteer, which is geolocated and linked to Werner's HGIS (and =
Geonames). We would prefer to have it as a separate dataset in WHG =
(keeping of course links to HGIS).
>=20
> As you can imagine, many places in Alcedo have not yet been =
geolocated. We have set up a web interface to allow experts to =
contribute, but as with all projects of this kind, it is an ongoing =
effort.
>=20
> Looking forward to hearing your thoughts!
>=20
> Sorry for the long mail, I will be more available in April to discuss =
if you like, especially to discuss a plan to convert the data and check =
output.
>=20
> best,
> Carmen
> PS : My EHESS address has problems today, this is why I use my gmail =
address..


